'''Imperial officers''' were individuals who held a position of authority and responsibility in the [[Imperial Military|military forces]], and some civilian elements, of the [[Galactic Empire]].

When the Empire succeeded the [[Galactic Republic]] after the end of the [[Clone Wars]], most [[officer]]s were tasked with overseeing the [[Imperial Army]] and [[Imperial Navy|Navy]], while some lead the [[stormtrooper]]s, shock [[troop]]s of the [[New Order|new regime]].

After the signing of the [[Galactic Concordance]], Imperial officers were made illegal as part of the disarmament and any who did not adhere to the terms of surrender to the [[New Republic]] were classified as war criminals. 

==Overview==
{{Quote|I am an ''Imperial officer''. I do not tolerate disrespect, ''my love''.|Captain Cerasus Ehllo, to his wife Aryssha Starros|<ref name="Sana Starros 1">[[Sana Starros 1|''Sana Starros'' 1]]</ref>}}
[[File:SWE-Jerjerrod.png|thumb|left|240px|[[Tiaan Jerjerrod]], a Moff and officer in service to the Galactic Empire]]
[[Officer]]s were high-class [[soldier]]s who held various positions of responsibility, authority, and duty within the various branches of [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Imperial Military|armed forces]]. Common traits among those officers were ambition, ruthlessness, and strong approval of [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine's]] plans to destroy the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|rebellion]].<ref name="SWCT">{{SWCT|set=Base Series 1|cardname=Imperial Officer - Soldier}}</ref> Since its creation, the Empire inherited a complex military hierarchy, within which many Imperial officers discovering that most of them were permitted promotions. This created a culture of shifting blame on others for mistakes and attempting to avoid exposure of committing unprincipled actions. Officers understood that exploiting the mistakes of others was a way to advance their own careers.<ref name="Imperial Officers and Agents">{{EncyclopediaCite|Imperial Officers and Agents}}</ref> Pride and ego resulted in situations where a new [[commanding officer]] would order changes to their command, such as changes for what was allowed aboard a [[starship]], entirely to wipe away traces of the preceding [[commander]] and the culture they had instilled.<ref name="Thrawn">[[Thrawn (novel)|''Thrawn'']]</ref>

Among these officers were those Imperial who authentically believed in the legitimacy of the Galactic Empire, and sought to expand its influence in the galaxy, as well as those who joined the Imperial Military with the intention of earning a comfortable livelihood at the expense of the Empire's opponents.<ref name="Imperial Officers and Agents" /> The upper echelons of the Empire included those whose influential families afforded them preferred treatment and advancement. Officers were put through one of several prestigious academies across [[the galaxy]] that raised ambitious men and women who would perfectly echo the Imperial mantra of control through authority. As the line between the Imperial [[Politics|political]] machine and Imperial war machine became more blurred, the Empire so gradually transformed into [[stratocracy]] that many in the [[galaxy]] simply took no notice.<ref name="Rogue One UVG">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref>

Since the Empire favored [[human]]s at the expense of [[alien]]s,<ref name="Rebels Visual Dictionary">''[[Star Wars Rebels: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> the ranks of its officers were dominated by the former.<ref name="Epic Battles">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Visual Guide: Epic Battles]]''</ref> Additionally, most of those holding [[Military rank|high ranks]] were [[Gender|males]].<ref name="Smuggler's Run">''[[Smuggler's Run: A Han Solo & Chewbacca Adventure]]''</ref> One notable exception to the Empire's humanocentrism was [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo]], a [[Chiss]] who was eventually promoted to the military rank of [[Grand Admiral]].<ref name="Steps Into Shadow">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Steps Into Shadow]]''</ref> Imperial officers wore a [[Imperial military uniforms|uniform]] that consisted of a double-breasted [[Clothing|tunic]] with matching trousers, a pair of [[Color|black]] [[boot]]s, a [[belt]] and an [[Imperial kepi]] [[Hat|command cap]]. There were regulations that made sure all officers maintained a neatly groomed appearance while wearing their uniforms.<ref name="Tark">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref>

[[File:Imperial_Army_trooper.png|thumb|right|300px|An Imperial officer in [[Imperial officer battle armor|combat gear]]]]
Although officers often cut their [[hair]] short for optimal efficiency, all were permitted to keep it long on the condition that they wore it pinned back in tight braids. This allowed [[Nash Windrider]], a male officer from [[Alderaan]], to retain a traditional hairstyle from his [[homeworld]].<ref name="Lost Stars">''[[Lost Stars]]''</ref> In addition to those officers who exerted command in the [[Imperial Navy|Navy]] or the [[Imperial Army|Army]], there were other specializations. [[Loyalty officer]]s,<ref name="Aftermath">[[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']]</ref> also known as Security Officers, were tasked with identifying and culling any seditious individual within the Empire's own ranks.<ref name="SWCT" /> The Galactic Empire made an effort to identify recruits in its [[Imperial Academy|Imperial Academies]] who were potential officer material. Recruits identified to potentially have such talent were sometimes sent to specialized officer academies, such as the [[Arkanis Academy|academy]] on [[Arkanis]].<ref name="secret">''[[Servants of the Empire: The Secret Academy]]''</ref>

As noted by Captain [[Raymus Antilles]] of the [[Royal Alderaan Civil Fleet|Alderaan fleet]], Imperial officers were generally inflexible in their decision making and thought processes.<ref name="Princess of Alderaan" /> Imperial captain [[Cerasus Ehllo]] made it a point to not accept any form of perceived disrespect, even if it came from his wife [[Aryssha Starros]], because of his status as an Imperial officer.<ref name="Sana Starros 1" /> Former [[scout trooper]] [[Khu Fornot]] held a low opinion of Imperial officers, believing that they lied to "grunts" like himself all while offloading "the real work" onto them. [[Tern Koyatta]], an Imperial [[technician]] who posed as a general, claimed in response that an Imperial officer only withheld information if it was something their subordinates did not need to know.<ref name="Ewoks 4">[[Ewoks (2024) 4|''Ewoks'' (2024) 4]]</ref> Indeed, Thrawn once reflected how a commander would not always share every detail of their plan to their subordinates, yet obedience needed to follow no matter what in order for the whole unit to achieve victory.<ref name="Thrawn" />

==History==
===Imperial control===
[[File:LtOicunn.png|thumb|left|250px|Imperial officers were the successors of the regular, non-Jedi officers of the Galactic Republic.]]
At the end of the [[Clone Wars]], [[Supreme Chancellor|Chancellor]] Sheev Palpatine, leader of the Republic, unilaterally [[Proclamation of the New Order|reorganized]] the regime into an autocratic Galactic Empire and also [[Order 66|ordered]] the [[Great Jedi Purge|extermination]] of all [[Jedi]].<ref name="ROTS" /> The [[Republic Military]] was then reformed into the Imperial Military. Although most of the Imperial leadership, in particular that of the military, hailed from the [[Core Worlds]] and [[Inner Rim Territories|Inner Rim]], the [[heart]] of the Empire, there was room for mobility. [[Wilhuff Tarkin]], who became the Empire's first [[Grand Moff]], was [[Reproduction|born]] on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[Planet|world]] of [[Eriadu]], which, before the rise of the Empire, was not a particularly well-known world.<ref name="Tark" /> Although it was [[Annexation of Jelucan|annexed]] by the Empire during the height of its reign, the planet [[Jelucan]], a world of poor [[farmer]]s and minor [[noble]]s, provided several prominent officers, such as [[Thane Kyrell|Thane]] and [[Dalven Kyrell|Dalven]] of the [[Kyrell family]] and the peasant [[Ciena Ree]].<ref name="Lost Stars" />

Due to resentment towards alien species because of the many aliens whom had participated in the [[Separatist Crisis|Separatist Movement]], very few found it easy to serve as officers in the military, mostly serving as low-ranking servicemen, noncombatants, and occasionally in government positions. However, there were few exceptions. The Chiss Mitth'raw'nuruodo, better known by his [[core name]] "Thrawn," was one of them, having attended the [[Royal Imperial Academy]] on Palpatine's personal order. Although initially unpopular with the [[Admiralty (Imperial)|Imperial Admiralty]] for his unconventional tactics, he ultimately became highly regarded to a few of his peers, being promoted to Grand Admiral and given command of the [[Seventh Fleet (Galactic Empire)|Seventh Fleet]]. Ironically, he had only accepted his commission as a means to infiltrate the Empire in order to assess its might, as his fellow leaders in the [[Chiss Ascendancy]], where his true loyalties laid, believed that it could make a powerful ally against or distraction for the looming threats in the [[Unknown Regions]],<ref name="Thrawn" /> chief among them the [[Grysk Hegemony]].<ref name="Lesser Evil">''[[Thrawn Ascendancy: Lesser Evil]]''</ref>

The Empire did not shy away from welcoming colonials from the fringes into their ranks either, although they did not often garner as much respect from their superiors, meaning that they had to work extra hard if they were to rise through the ranks. [[Lieutenant Commander]] [[Eli N. Vanto|Eli Vanto]] was born on the planet of [[Lysatra]], which was deep in [[Wild Space]], near the Unknown Regions, where the Empire's influence was scarce. Vanto ultimately gained admission into the Royal Imperial Academy on [[Coruscant]] and became one of the most prominent officers in the Seventh Fleet under Thrawn, serving as [[First Mate|second in command]] aboard the [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|Star Destroyer]] ''[[Chimaera]]''.<ref name="Thrawn" />

[[File:TalaDurith-Databank.jpg|thumb|right|270px|Tala Durith, an Imperial officer turned defector]]
One Imperial officer, a [[captain]]<ref name="Rank">{{ImperialRanks-PreDS-LA}}</ref> named [[Tala Durith]], joined the Empire on the hope she could bring positive change. However, an [[Execution of Force-sensitive individuals on Garel|execution of Force-sensitive families]] on<ref name="Kenobi V">{{Kenobi|Part V}}</ref> the planet<ref name="Garel">{{Databank|garel|Garel}}</ref> [[Garel]] convinced her the Empire did not stand for the ideals she had joined for. Before the execution, she had even been told the families she helped arrest had simply not paid taxes. The execution convinced her to abandon the Empire and help the [[Hidden Path]] group,<ref name="Kenobi V" /> which worked to help Force-sensitives escape Imperial reach. Working undercover, she served as an officer in the [[Mapuzo|Imperial detachment]] that maintained control over the mining planet [[Mapuzo]], where she helped many Force-sensitives escape. Ultimately, she helped [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] escape Mapuzo<ref name="Kenobi III">{{Kenobi|Part III}}</ref> in [[9 BBY]]<ref name="9 BBY Date">{{KenobiDate|III}}</ref> and again went undercover to help Kenobi infiltrate [[Fortress Inquisitorius]] to [[Rescue of Princess Leia (9 BBY)|rescue]] [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]].<ref name="Kenobi IV">{{Kenobi|Part IV}}</ref>

===Empire at war===
{{Quote|Eyes on an officer.|Del Meeko|<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Disciplined-SASP.png|thumb|left|270px|The Imperial losses sustained in the Battles of Yavin and Endor both resulted in younger officers being promoted.]]
Prior to the outbreak of the [[Galactic Civil War]], there were more [[captain]]s, lieutenant commanders, and [[commander]]s than there were [[Starship|ships]] in the navy, meaning that the younger and more inexperienced officers, particularly those who had joined after the Proclamation of a New Order or had not served in the Clone Wars, either served in positions that they were overqualified for or were inactive altogether.<ref name="A New Dawn">[[A New Dawn (novel)|''A New Dawn'']]</ref> That changed after the [[Battle of Yavin|destruction]] of the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]], which left a power-vacuum in the high command. As such, many younger officers were promoted. The same exact thing happened after the Emperor's [[death]] at the [[Battle of Endor]].<ref name="Lost Stars" /> In the time after the Battle of Endor, the Imperial turncoat [[Ralsius Paldora]] noted that 1 in every 148 Imperial officers would surrender to the [[New Republic]] and sought asylum.<ref name="Battlefront II" />

===Collapse of the Empire===
Contrary to how it was two decades earlier, many younger, under-qualified officers as young as in their early twenties were promoted and given command of their own ships, even Star Destroyers, as was the case when Ciena Ree was promoted to commander and given captaincy of the Star Destroyer ''[[Inflictor]]'' shortly before the [[Battle of Jakku]].<ref name="Lost Stars" /> With much of the leadership destroyed either over Endor or during the [[rebellion on Akiva]],<ref name="Aftermath" /> the government slowly lost much of its power. The military took control over the Empire, effectively transitioning it into a stratocracy under the command of [[Fleet Admiral]] [[Gallius Rax]] and his [[Shadow Council]]. Despite this, some greedy Imperial officers would try to seize power for themselves or take their forces and leave the Empire altogether, hoping to build factions of their own.<ref name="Life Debt">''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]''</ref>

[[File:Strength_Through_Order.png|thumb|right|250px|Grand Admiral Rae Sloane, new leader of the Empire]]
Rax, after declaring himself [[Counselor to the Empire]],<ref name="Life Debt" /> would then unite the Empire and lead them to [[Jakku]], where they made one final stand against the New Republic, which proved to be a devastating loss for the Empire. After the Empire's defeat on Jakku, its leadership, under [[Grand Vizier]] [[Mas Amedda]], signed the [[Galactic Concordance]] with the New Republic. The conditions of the surrender placed various restraints on the weakened Empire. One of these conditions stated that those Imperial officers who did not repent for their actions were to be branded as war criminals.<ref name="Empire's End">''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]''</ref> Despite this formality, the Imperial Navy was still permitted to remain organized, so long as it relocated to the [[Inner systems' Imperial remnant|Imperial remnant]] established in the Core and the Inner Rim.<ref name="Lost Stars" />

In secret, [[Grand Admiral]] [[Rae Sloane]] took charge of Palpatine's [[Contingency]] from Rax in order to reform the Empire in the image of what she envisioned it as being.<ref name="Empire's End" /> Indeed, some staunch Imperial officers refused to accept defeat, affiliating themselves with a militarized faction of the Empire that locked itself into a [[Cold War]] with the New Republic. Eventually, many would relocate their forces to the Unknown Regions,<ref name="TFA Visual Dictionary">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> where Sloane began building her [[Unknown Regions Imperial remnant|Imperial remnant]] in the months following the Battle of Jakku.<ref name="Empire's End" /> The Imperial forces in the Unknown Regions would help establish the [[First Order military|military]] of the [[First Order]].<ref name="TFA Visual Dictionary" />

==Equipment==
===Uniform===
Imperial officers wore a [[Imperial officer's uniform|uniform]] comprised of a [[Imperial military uniforms#Design|tunic]], pants, [[Imperial kepi|cap]], belt, boots, and occasionally gloves; the former three of which often varied in [[color]], depending on the officer's branch and duties. [[Rank insignia plaque]]s were located on the tunic's upper-lefthand chest, and one or mode [[code cylinder]]s were placed inside of each breast pocket. If the situation required it, officers could don armor and a helmet, to protect their body, head, and neck.<ref name="ESB">{{Film|V}}</ref>

===Weapons===
[[File:RK-3_BF2.png|right|thumb|200px|RK-3 blasters were the Imperial officer's primary weapon]]
Officers used [[SE-14r light repeating blaster]]s,<ref name="Kenobi III" /> [[RK-3 blaster]]s, [[DH-17 blaster pistol]]s, [[DL-44 heavy blaster pistol]]s, and [[DT-29 heavy blaster pistol]]s. They were also equipped with [[flash grenade]]s and a [[disruptor]] able to incapacitate enemy weapons. In battle, officers carried [[Squad shield|portable shield generators]] or [[turret]]s.<ref name="Battlefront II" /> Officers could also wield an electrified [[baton]].<ref name="Customized">{{AtomicMassGames|url=character/customizable-imperial-officer-agent|text=SWQ09 Customizable Imperial Officer and Agent}}</ref>

